# UI-WINDOW-1 fix round R1 (F2), R2: closing the construction menu turns off a building tool a cell
# armed, by both routes - another tab (the bust, reference centre 870 212; since R2 a click on the
# construction tab itself, already selected, changes nothing) and Esc. After each
# close, a click on the tile construction_menu_arm.script builds on (1156 516, free and buildable
# for type 501 on lan5's developer island) posts no command: the latest outcome stays none. Before
# the fix the tool stayed armed (DevTool::arm sets it on) and that click built the house.
# Launch: --play data/maps/lan5.txt --construction-menu on --layout data/ui
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
click_px 809 212
wait frames 5
click_px 833 330
wait frames 5
expect title build 501
click_px 809 212
wait frames 5
expect title build 501
expect fact ui.tab == construction
click_px 870 212
wait frames 5
expect fact ui.tab == player_list
expect title-lacks build 501
click 1156 516
wait frames 10
expect outcome none
key b
wait frames 5
click_px 833 330
wait frames 5
expect title build 501
key esc
wait frames 5
expect title-lacks build 501
click 1156 516
wait frames 10
expect outcome none
quit
